notes: Architecture-first DMMW slice the founder asked for ("optimierter Architektur"). Introduces the single authoritative musical clock as the live backbone: PatternEngine still owns the real-time timer but now RELAYS every pulse (tick/play/stop/tempo/swing) into Transport, so musical position/tempo/play-state live in ONE observable place that the timeline, MIDI clock and Ableton Link can all ride in later cycles (Cycle 1 — zero audible change; existing onStep/onTick stay the live path). Transport gets its first real consumer: the Arrangement timeline now shows a LIVE bar·beat playhead (monospaced, 1-based) while the song plays — you can see where you are in the arrangement. Foundation-only relay test runs on Linux CI (tempo/swing clamp relay, play/stop + position reset, no-transport no-op). Both gates green.
